<rml>
<head>
    <title>Launch</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="frame">
        <div class="case window">

            <!-- The lid is the window's title bar: the mark and the title, then our own
                 minimize and close. The band is draggable (main/launch.cpp's hit test). -->
            <div class="lid">
                <div class="head">
                    <div class="mark"></div>
                    <div class="title">OoT: Recompiled</div>
                </div>
                <div class="chrome">
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-min"><div class="glyph-min"></div></div>
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-max"><div class="glyph-max"></div></div>
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-close"><div class="glyph-x"><div class="bar a"></div><div class="bar b"></div></div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- THE ROWS ARE BUILT FROM THE MODEL, NOT LISTED HERE, exactly as the controls
                 document and the debug menu build theirs. This used to be a fixed run of row
                 elements, and on 2026-09-22 adding two settings pushed three rows off the end of
                 it: a row with no element simply does not appear, so Controls, Your files and
                 Debug vanished while the menu looked perfectly normal. Slots were added, and then
                 the user asked the better question ("but can we not just add scrollable areas?"),
                 which is this. There is now no number here to get wrong, and a list longer than
                 the case scrolls instead of being cut off. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="launch-rows"></div>

            <!-- Play and Quit are ACTIONS, not settings, and the user asked twice for them to
                 look like it: out of the list, under a divider, Quit on the left as a secondary
                 and Play on the right as the primary. They keep their place in the keyboard and
                 pad order; only where they are drawn has changed. -->
            <div class="actions">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="act-quit"><span class="act-label" id="act-quit-label">Quit</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-play" id="act-play"><span class="act-label" id="act-play-label">Play</span></div>
            </div>

            <!-- ONE foot row (the user, 2026-09-20: "it's just a single row"). The key hints
                 on the left; the version and what Windows says of this program's own file
                 together on the right, as one clickable thing that opens About. The ROM blurb
                 that used to sit left of the hints is gone: the ROM row already says it. -->
            <div class="foot">
                <span id="launch-foot">F2 is about, F3 is controls</span>
                <span class="link" id="launch-signed">Not signed</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
